hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"153","Narrated to me: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, Narrated to me Ibn Ulayya, Narrated to us Muhammad bin Ishaq, Narrated to me Muhammad bin Talha bin Yazid bin Rukana, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ali entered my house, and he had urinated, so he called for ablution, so we brought him a bowl that would take the tide or His relative, until it was placed in his hands, and he said: O Ibn Abbas, shall I not perform ablution for you as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? So I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: “So he put a vessel for him and washed his hands, then he rinsed his mouth, sniffed and exhaled, then took it with his right hand, meaning Water and he covered his face with it.” He mentioned the hadith"
